  "id": "task-switching",
  "term": "task switching",
  "definition": "Task switching is a task paradigm in which a person changes from one task to another. Research described here treats it as involving control of the current task set, such as reconfiguring the active rules or overcoming carryover from the previous task, although some versions may instead be completed through learned cue-target associations.",
